                <pb facs="0839" n="741" sameAs="frus:frus1900/pg741"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 5.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Extract from minutes of San Francisco board of health,
                        held on the evening of May 18, 1900.</hi></head>
                <p>“Dr. Baum introduced the following resolution:</p>
                <p>“‘<hi rendition="#italic">Resolved</hi>, That it is the sense of this board that
                    bubonic plague exists in the city and county of San Francisco, and that all
                    necessary steps already taken for the prevention of its spread be continued,
                    together with such additional measures as may be required.’</p>
                <p>“Seconded by Dr. Bazet and unanimously adopted.”</p>
                <p>Respectfully transmitted to Count Mutsu, Imperial consul-general, San Francisco,
                    Cal.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">J. J. Kinyoun</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Surgeon, M. H. S.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
